    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103054" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τέμπ-εα</span></b> , 
			contr.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τέμπη</span></b> , τά, <u>Tempe</u>, the valley between Mounts Olympus and
		Ossa, through which the Peneus escapes into the sea, <i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
			7.173
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Call.
			<u>Del.</u>
			105
		</span></i>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>any sequestered vale</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Cic.
				<u>Att.</u>
				4.15.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.P.
				219
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				916
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				1017
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἢ κατὰ Πηνειῶ καλὰ τέμπεα, ἢ κατὰ
					Πίνδω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					1.67
				</span></i>
			: also in late Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Aristid.
				<u>Or.</u>
				23(42).20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				36(48).120
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				16
			</span></i>.</div>
